      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes its mandatory.\n\nReason:\nLets say we comment it out, the build fails as below:\n\n```\nERROR at //build/toolchain/embedded.gni:305:35: No value named \"memory_alloc\" in scope \"invoker\" plat_memory_alloc \u003d invoker.memory_alloc ^----------- See //build/toolchain/embedded.gni:333:3: whence it was called. aarch64_common_toolchain(\"${target_name}\") { ^------------------------------------------- See //build/toolchain/embedded.gni:342:3: whence it was called. aarch64_toolchain(\"${target_name}\") { ^------------------------------------ See //project/reference/BUILD.gn:181:1: whence it was called. aarch64_toolchains(\"aem_v8a_fvp_vhe\") { ^-------------------------------------- See //BUILD.gn:12:12: which caused the file to be included. deps \u003d [ \"//project/${project}:root\" ] ^-------------------------- make: *** [Makefile:119: out/reference/build.ninja] Error 1\n\n```\n\nThis implies that the template requires memory_alloc to be passed explicitly.\nIt has no default value and the global plat_memory_alloc only works after we pass this param explicitly for each toolchain.\n\nSee this line in (embedded.gni) file:\n      plat_memory_alloc \u003d invoker.memory_alloc\n  \nThe template in embedded.gni requires every toolchain to pass a memory_alloc parameter.\nIf its omitted, GN fails with: “No value named memory_alloc in scope invoker.”\nSo specifying memory_alloc \u003d \"//src/memory_alloc:memory_alloc\" is mandatory.\n\nHope this helps. Please close the comment, if you are ok with it.",
